---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';

const title = 'Terms and Conditions | WordPress Development Services | ElPuas Digital Crafts';
const description = 'Read our terms and conditions for WordPress development, WooCommerce solutions, and white-label web services. Clear policies for our digital craftsmanship services.';
const lang = 'en';
---

<Layout {title} {description} {lang}>
    <section class="container">
        <h1>Terms and Conditions</h1>
        <p>Last updated: 29/10/2026</p>
        <p>Legal Entity: <span class="accent">ElPuas Artesanos Digitales S.A.</span></p>
    </section>

    <h2>1. Introduction</h2>
    <p>These Terms and Conditions (“Terms”) govern the services provided by <span class="accent">ElPuas Digital Crafts</span>, the commercial brand of <span class="accent">ElPuas Artesanos Digitales S.A.</span>, including monthly support plans, web development projects, and related digital services.</p>
    <p>By engaging with our services, you agree to these Terms in full.</p>

    <h2>2. Scope of Services</h2>
    <h3>A. Monthly Plans</h3>
    <p>All monthly plans include a WordPress website built with a premium theme adapted to the client's brand, the licenses needed for the site, and ongoing maintenance. The adapted template is not a fully custom build.</p>
    <p>All plans include:</p>
    <ul>
        <li>WordPress core, theme, and plugin updates</li>
        <li>Regular backups</li>
        <li>Security monitoring</li>
        <li>Technical support by email</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Additional scope depends on the plan:</p>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>Essential ($150/month):</strong> the adapted premium-theme website and licenses, maintenance, backups, security, monitoring, and email support. Hosting and monthly development hours after delivery are not included.</li>
        <li><strong>Growth ($180/month):</strong> everything in Essential, plus hosting, 4 development hours per month, performance optimization, and monthly reports.</li>
        <li><strong>AI Commerce ($250/month):</strong> everything in Growth, with 8 total development hours per month, plus the AI services and text allowance described in Section 3.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>The included site scope, including pages, products, and integrations, is confirmed before subscribing. Additional features and work are assessed within available hours where applicable or quoted separately.</p>
    <p>Hosting is included only in Growth and AI Commerce. All plans include licenses needed for the site; other third-party services or subscriptions are specified in the proposal.</p>
    <p>Slack is not included generally; it is available only when confirmed in writing as part of the contracted service or onboarding.</p>

    <h3>B. Project-Based Custom Development</h3>
    <p>Custom development is quoted separately and defined in a written proposal or scope document.</p>
    <p>This includes:</p>
    <ul>    <li>Fully custom WordPress themes</li>
        <li>WooCommerce integrations</li>
        <li>Headless or hybrid frontend builds</li>
        <li>API development and 3rd-party integrations</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Each project is unique and includes specific deliverables, timelines, and pricing as defined in your signed proposal.</p>


    <h2>3. Artificial Intelligence Services</h2>
    <p>The AI Commerce plan includes up to <strong>3,000,000 text tokens per month</strong> and AI functionality integrated directly into the client’s WordPress website.</p>
    <p>The monthly text-token allowance may be used only for enabled text functions, including:</p>
    <ul>
        <li>Product descriptions</li>
        <li>SEO titles and meta descriptions</li>
        <li>Blog articles</li>
        <li>Content rewriting and optimization</li>
        <li>Content translation</li>
        <li>Text used in agreed editorial automations</li>
    </ul>
    <p>AI Commerce also includes configured functions for marketing images and WordPress automation. The 3,000,000 tokens apply only to text and do not convert into image credits or a number of images.</p>
    <p>The image provider, usage policy, limits, and applicable costs must be confirmed in writing before activation. Included automations are limited to workflows agreed during onboarding. External API, CRM, ERP, platform, and customer-system integrations are quoted separately.</p>
    <p>The allowance does not cover:</p>
    <ul>
        <li>AI chatbots, customer support assistants, or public-facing conversational interfaces</li>
        <li>Custom AI agents</li>
        <li>Third-party API consumption or general AI usage outside the website</li>
        <li>Video or audio generation</li>
        <li>Speech-to-text or text-to-speech services</li>
        <li>Any AI service not explicitly included in the subscribed plan</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Token consumption varies depending on the requested task. If the monthly allowance is exceeded, additional usage may be quoted separately and will only be activated after client approval.</p>
    <p>EPDC may change the underlying AI provider—including OpenAI, Anthropic, Google, or an equivalent technology—without affecting the service, provided equivalent functionality is maintained.</p>

    <h2>4. Support Hours</h2>
    <p>Standard support: <span class="accent">Monday to Friday, 9am–5pm (EST)</span> for clients in the USA, EU, and LATAM</p>
    <p>Emergency support: by email for active plans; Slack only when included in writing in the contracted service</p>
    <p>Off-hour work may incur additional charges</p>

    <h2>5. Use of Development Hours</h2>
    <p>Growth includes <strong>4 development hours per month</strong> and AI Commerce includes <strong>8 total hours per month</strong>. Essential does not include monthly development hours.</p>
    <ul>
        <li>Hours <span class="accent">do not roll over</span> month to month</li>
        <li>Complex features or large redesigns are not included</li>
        <li>Overage hours will be quoted and approved separately</li>
        <li>Tasks are scheduled in order of receipt unless marked urgent</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>6. Client Responsibilities</h2>
    <p>Clients must:</p>
    <ul>
        <li>Provide all necessary content (images, text, brand assets) in a timely manner</li>
        <li>Respond to communications within a reasonable timeframe (max 5 business days)</li>
        <li>Maintain valid login credentials and access to relevant services</li>
        <li>Follow best practices and technical guidance from ElPuas Digital Crafts</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Delays caused by lack of client input may affect delivery timelines.</p>

    <h2>7. Payments & Renewals</h2>
    <ul>
        <li>All plans are <span class="accent">prepaid monthly</span> and invoiced within the first <span class="accent">fifteen (15) days of each month</span>.</li>
        <li>If payment is <span class="accent">not received within 45 calendar days</span> from the invoice date, <span class="accent">we reserve the right to disable the website</span> and suspend any associated services without further notice.</li>
        <li>Service reactivation may incur additional fees.</li>
        <li>Project-based invoices are due according to agreed milestones (typically 50/50)</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>8. Limitations & Exclusions</h2>
    <p>Unless otherwise stated, our services <span class="accent">do not include</span>:</p>
    <ul>
        <li>Full redesigns, fully custom development, or additional sites outside the contracted scope</li>
        <li>Human content creation (copywriting, translations, photography, etc.), except for the AI-assisted functions described for AI Commerce in Section 3</li>
        <li>SEO audits, paid campaigns, or advertising management</li>
        <li>Recovery from hacks due to client negligence</li>
        <li>Support for unauthorized or pirated third-party plugins</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>9. Intellectual Property</h2>
    <ul>
        <li>Custom code and designs are transferred to the client upon full payment</li>
        <li>Themes, templates, and third-party plugins remain under their respective licenses</li>
        <li>Clients are responsible for acquiring licenses for any premium content not included in the scope</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>10. Emergency Policy</h2>
    <p>Critical issues (site down, security breaches) will be prioritized by email or, when included in writing, through the dedicated Slack channel.</p>
    <p>Non-critical issues will be handled during standard hours.</p>

    <h2>11. Confidentiality</h2>

    <p>Both parties agree to maintain confidentiality regarding proprietary information, credentials, internal processes, and client data. This obligation survives the termination of our agreement.</p>

    <h2>12. Limitation of Liability</h2>

    <p><span class="accent">ElPuas Digital Crafts is not liable</span> for indirect, incidental, or consequential damages arising from service use, including loss of business, revenue, or data. Total liability is limited to the amount paid for the service in question.</p>

    <h2>13. Termination</h2>

    <p>We reserve the right to terminate services:</p>
    <ul>
        <li>Immediately for non-payment or breach of agreement</li>
        <li>With 15 days' notice if the client repeatedly delays or obstructs project delivery</li>
    </ul>

    <p>Clients may cancel at any time with proper notice. No refunds are provided for unused service periods.</p>

    <h2>14. Force Majeure</h2>

    <p>Neither party shall be liable for failure to fulfill obligations caused by events beyond reasonable control (natural disasters, war, pandemics, service provider outages, etc.)</p>

    <h2>15. Governing Law</h2>

    <p>These Terms are governed by the laws of <span class="accent">Costa Rica</span>, and any disputes shall be resolved under the jurisdiction of the local courts, unless otherwise agreed.</p>

    <h2>16. Contact</h2>

    <p><span class="accent">ElPuas Digital Crafts</span></p>

    <p>Legal Entity: <span class="accent">ElPuas Artesanos Digitales S.A.</span></p>

    <p>Email: <a href="mailto:management@elpuasdev.com">management@elpuasdev.com</a></p>

    <p>Slack access depends on the contracted service and must be confirmed in writing during onboarding.</p>

    <p>This document may be updated periodically. Clients will be notified of major changes in writing.</p>
    <div class="spacer"></div>
</Layout>

<style>
    .accent {
        color: var(--color-tertiary);
        font-size: inherit;
    }

    ul, p, h3, h2 {
        margin-top: 0;
        margin-bottom: var(--space-md);
    }

    h2 {
        margin-top: var(--space-2xl);
        font-size: var(--fontsize-h3);
    }

    h3 {
        font-size: var(--fontsize-h4);
        font-weight: 400;
        letter-spacing: 0;
    }

    p {
        margin-top: 0;
    }

    ul {
        list-style: square;
        padding-left: var(--space-2xl);

        li::marker {
            color: var(--color-tertiary);
        }
    }

    .spacer {
        margin-top: var(--space-4xl);
    }
</style>
